.Dd October 5, 2026
.Dt AUDIO-OUTPUT-TOGGLE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm audio-output-toggle
.Nd cycle the default audio output
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
cycles the default playback device through the playable outputs
from
.Xr audio-output-devices 1 ,
then a combined sink that plays them all, then back to the first.
The usual chord is the media key
.Pq Fn+F12 .
.Pp
The glyph is
.Xr audio-output-osd 1 :
speakers, headphones, headphones with a count when more than two
outputs are playable, or speakers with an All badge for the
combined sink.
.Xr volume-osd 1
then follows the newly selected sink.
.Pp
A held key steps the glyph once per press.
One applier catches up to the latest choice.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "BHOTKEYS_GREETER"
.It Ev AUDIO_ALL_SINK
Name of the combined Pulse sink.
The default is
.Cm combined_all .
.It Ev DISPLAY
X server.
The default is
.Pa :0 .
.It Ev PULSE_SERVER
Pulse socket.
.It Ev BHOTKEYS_GREETER
When set, the system Pulse socket is used.
.It Ev HOME
Directory above
.Pa .cache/audio-output-cycle .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.cache/audio-output-cycle"
.It Pa ~/.cache/audio-output-cycle
Latest cycle choice.
.It Pa /tmp/audio-output-toggle.lock
Lock around one cycle.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr audio-output-devices 1 ,
.Xr audio-output-osd 1 ,
.Xr bhotkeys 1 ,
.Xr volume-osd 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
